===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, [[relate|relating]] to, [[consist]]ing of, or [[use#Verb|used]] in a [[ceremony]].
#: {{synonyms|en|ceremonious|formal|ritual|ritualistic}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|act=III|scene=ii|passage=What mockery will it be / To want the bridegroom when the priest attends / To speak the '''ceremonial''' rites of marriage!}}
#* {{RQ:Johnson Rambler|date=3 December 1751|issue=179|page=53|passage=His merit introduced him to ſplendid tables and elegant acquaintance, but he did not find himſelf alvvays qualified to join in the converſation. He vvas diſtreſſed by civilities, vvhich he knevv not hovv to repay, and entangled in many '''ceremonial''' perplexities, from vvhich his books and diagrams could not extricate him.}}
#* {{RQ:Hallam England|volume=I|chapter=II|passage=[T]his change in '''ceremonial''' observances and outward show was trifling when compared to that in the objects of worship {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1963|author=w:Sylvia Plath|chapter=15|title=w:The Bell Jar|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Bantam Books|year_published=1972|page=151|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/belljar00platrich|passage=Philomena Guinea's black Cadillac eased through the tight, five o'clock traffic like a '''ceremonial''' car.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} {{synonym of|en|ceremonious|t=of a [[person#Noun|person]]: [[fond#Adjective|fond]] of ceremony or ritual, or of [[observe|observing]] [[strict]] [[etiquette]] or [[formality]]; [[punctilious]]}}
#* {{RQ:Donne Poems|Satyre I|page=326|passage=Oh monstrous, superstitious puritan, / Of refin’d manners, yet '''ceremoniall''' man, {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Juvenal Satires|satire=10|lines=56-57|page=193|passage=[W]ith dumb Pride, and a set formal Face, / He moves, in the dull '''Ceremonial''' track, {{...}}}}

